  "blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": 0,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "After turning on the motor, software must further wait for \none half second (500ms), or for the DSKRDY* line to go low.\n",
      "bbox": [
        219.94000244140625,
        68.46501922607422,
        492.57244873046875,
        92.16399383544922
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.36606027692607446,
        0.08869904492016041,
        0.8198199735696844,
        0.11940197084058633
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 1,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PB6 \nDSKSEL3*\nSelect drive 3 (active low).\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.30999755859375,
        107.31298065185547,
        337.4014587402344,
        117.96300506591797
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14365127424332327,
        0.13902806132171777,
        0.5615589253920079,
        0.15282557433759048
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PB5 \nDSKSEL2*\nSelect drive 2 (active low).\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.30999755859375,
        132.9129638671875,
        337.4539794921875,
        143.51300048828125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14365127424332327,
        0.17219381643052986,
        0.5616463390538744,
        0.1859265683531594
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 3,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PB4 \nDSKSEL1*\nSelect drive 1 (active low).\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.30999755859375,
        158.81195068359375,
        337.4595031738281,
        169.31195068359375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14365127424332327,
        0.20574694211402034,
        0.5616555324721183,
        0.21935009277678963
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 4,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PB3 \nDSKSELO*\nSelect drive 0 (internal drive) (active low).\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.5099868774414,
        184.61090087890625,
        405.83990478515625,
        195.2109375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14398412931573845,
        0.23917046653765056,
        0.6754654282268822,
        0.2529032184602801
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 5,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PB2 \nDSKSIDE\nSpecify which disk head to use. Zero indicates the upper head. \nDSKSIDE must be stable for 100 microseconds before writing. \nAfter writing, at least 1.3 milliseconds must pass before \nswitching DSKSIDE.\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.50997924804688,
        210.5098876953125,
        498.5233459472656,
        259.557861328125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14398411661764696,
        0.272723592221141,
        0.8297244341451071,
        0.3362671136526348
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 6,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PB1 \nDSKDIREC\nSpecify the direction to seek the heads. Zero implies \nseek towards the center spindle. Track zero is at the outside \nof the disk. This line must be set up before the actual step \npulse, with a separate write to the register.\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.50997924804688,
        274.70684814453125,
        485.32440185546875,
        324.35284423828125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14398411661764696,
        0.35589320413376624,
        0.8077565834779138,
        0.42021148648296025
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 7,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "PBO \nDSKSTEP*\nStep the heads of the disk. This signal must always be \nused as a quick pulse (high, momentarily low, then high).\n",
      "bbox": [
        86.79898071289062,
        339.5018615722656,
        471.25201416015625,
        362.85186767578125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14446512032355957,
        0.4398376165007786,
        0.784335004503759,
        0.4700884404057982
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 8,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "The drives used for the Amiga are guaranteed to get to the next \ntrack within 3 milliseconds. Some drives will support a much \nfaster rate, others will fail. Loops that decrement a counter \nto provide delay are not acceptable. See Appendix F \nfor a better solution.\n",
      "bbox": [
        219.98898315429688,
        377.90087890625,
        498.86883544921875,
        440.2489013671875
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.36614179867348623,
        0.48958500870044336,
        0.8302994545204647,
        0.5703592508968107
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 9,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "When reversing directions, a minimum of 18 milliseconds delay is \nrequired from the last step pulse. Settle time for Amiga drives \nis specified at 15 milliseconds.\n",
      "bbox": [
        220.48898315429688,
        455.6979064941406,
        513.75390625,
        491.8459167480469
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.36697398079784443,
        0.590374026547462,
        0.8550736342008974,
        0.6372051531801493
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 10,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "FLAG \nDSKINDEX*\nDisk index pulse ($BFDD00, bit 4). Can be used to \ncreate a level 6 interrupt. See Appendix F for details.\n",
      "bbox": [
        87.0789794921875,
        506.794921875,
        454.1734924316406,
        530.1449584960938
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.14493114028150553,
        0.6565721597516211,
        0.7559101235178914,
        0.6868230231933276
      ]
    },
